{"key":"73dea397a9ae19ce","source_file":"Potts St - Sy.json","source_id":29801,"source_url":"concordance-styx-ppl-styx","term":"Styx","headwords":["Styx","Stygian"],"latin":["Styx","Stygius"],"header_pairs":[{"english":["Styx"],"latin":["Styx"]},{"english":["Stygian"],"latin":["Stygius"]}],"header_sentences":[],"redirect_xref":null,"works":["AE","Coro","TCR"],"contexts":[{"reference":{"work":"TCR","section":"20","subsection":"end"},"text":"With such, everything of the Church is like the Styx or thick darkness in Tartarus.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"TCR","section":"119","subsection":"3"},"text":"The Heavens are then... suffocated by the evils which rise up, as by Stygian waters.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"TCR","section":"137","subsection":"2"},"text":"He has cast our faith into the Styx.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AE","section":"982","subsection":"end"},"text":"Such reasonings... are Stygian.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"Coro","section":"38","subsection":"end"},"text":"They called their Hells Tartaruses... and the deeps there the Styx.","comment":null,"footnote":null}],"slug":"styx","url":"/meta/potts/styx/"}